A '''Vampire Mask''' is a {{Rare}} [[Helmet]] obtained from [[Party Chests]] while {{NPCSprite|Foxy}} is in office with the {{AN|A Time for Giving}} perk active.

== Obtaining ==
A '''Vampire Mask''' can be obtained from [[Party Chests]] during the [[Spooky Festival]] while {{NPCSprite|Foxy}} is in office with the {{AN|A Time for Giving}} perk active.

== Usage ==
{{ItemInfo
|type = Helmet
|rarity = Rare
|defense = 111
|item_ability_name = Rejuvenate
|item_ability_desc = While wearing, drains {{Green|5}} health per second from all monsters within {{Yellow|8}} blocks.
}}
While the '''Vampire Mask''' is worn, all monsters within {{Green|8}} blocks are damaged for {{Stat|hp|5}} every second. The wearer heals for the amount the ability damages mobs. The ability does not trigger {{Ench|Thunderlord}} or {{Ench|Thunderbolt}}.

=== Crafting ===
{{Crafting Usage}}

== Trivia ==
* The '''Vampire Mask's''' ability triggers an additional hit on {{MobSprite|Zealot}}s, thus granting the {{Green|10%}} bonus Special Zealot chance.
* The '''Vampire Mask''' cannot be used on the {{zone|Private Island}}.
* The '''Vampire Mask''' used to be obtainable by placing in the top {{Green|10}} or by getting {{Green|2,000}} points or above in a [[Spooky Festival]] before October 30, 2020 before being replaced with the {{Item|Witch Mask}}.
** It was still possible to receive the '''Vampire Mask''' from the [[Spooky Festival]] after its replacement, but only during the bonus event from Mayor Foxy's perk, as it used the old system and rewards.

